yoyo undo --last-commit now exits 1 when git refuses to revert, and so does yoyo undo --all when its git checkout or git clean fails. I ran #1058's own reproduction (a repo with no author identity) on the built binary: same output as before, but exit 1 instead of 0. Build, all tests, clippy with -D warnings and the fmt check pass. Committed as 660b8e2e. It isn't pushed yet; the push will close #1058.

What changed
• The two functions that run git for undo now return both the note for the agent and whether git refused. The REPL's /undo only reads the note, so its output is unchanged.
• handle_undo_status returns 1 for a git refusal, 2 for a bad argument (as before), and 0 otherwise. I updated its doc comment.
• Each place that prints a git failure now sets the failure flag:
  • --last-commit: the git revert error.
  • --all: the git checkout -- . error, which stops early.
  • --all: the git clean -fd error. It carries on and still prints the ✓ line, so the REPL output stays exactly the same.

What's tested and what isn't
• Tested, in temp repos (new file `src/commands_git_undo_tests.rs`):
  • Reverting a merge commit, which git refuses without -m, gives 1, and HEAD doesn't move.
  • Reverting a plain commit gives 0, and the file really goes back.
  • A repo with no commits still gives 0.
• Checked the test catches the bug: when I forced the failure flag to false, the merge test failed. The code was restored in the same command and nothing was left in the file.
• Not tested: both `--all` failure paths. That code runs git in the current directory, and a test-only guard blocks checkout/clean from the project root. The change there is checked only by reading the code. The commit message and my comment on #1058 both say so.

Other edits
• I filed #1059. Outside a git repository, both --last-commit and --all print "nothing to undo" and exit 0, while diff, commit and blame exit 1 there. It's a different case from #1058 (git refusing to run vs. git failing), so the Fixes title stays accurate. One decision is still open: how to tell "not a repo" apart from "a repo with no commits".
• docs/src/usage/commands.md: the sentence saying a failed revert "still exits 0 (#1058)" now describes the new exit codes.
• ARCHITECTURE.md: new entry for this change.
• The size limit for commands_git.rs went from 3679 to 3722 lines (+43). It was a warning, not a failure, and I recorded the new size with a reason. The new tests went into a separate file so they don't count toward it.
• No user-facing text points at #1058 anymore. The three remaining mentions are code comments describing the fix.

